hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3037","**\nNarrated to us Muhammad ibn Maymun al-Jazzar, narrated to us Yahya ibn Abi al-Hajjaj, narrated to us ‘Awf, on the authority of al-Hasan who said:\nIt reached me that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said, “My father is an old man who has reached old age, embraced Islam, but has never performed Hajj nor is able to hold onto the riding animal. If I tie him to the riding animal, I fear I may kill him.”\nThe Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, “Perform Hajj on behalf of your father.”\n\n---"
"3038","Narrated to us Muhammad bin Mansur, who narrated to us Yahya bin Abi Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah (RA), from the Prophet (ﷺ), with a narration similar to the previous one, except that he said: \"The questioner asked about his mother.\""
